} \\geqslant \\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\frac{a(c-b)^{2}}{c+b}+\\frac{b(c-a)^{2}}{c+a}+\\frac{c(b-a)^{2}}{b+a}\\right]}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "1. Given the real numbers \\(a, b, c\\) such that \\(abc = 1\\), we need to prove:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{a^{3}(b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^{3}(c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^{3}(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\frac{a(c-b)^{2}}{c+b} + \\frac{b(c-a)^{2}}{c+a} + \\frac{c(b-a)^{2}}{b+a}\\right].\n   \\]\n\n2. Let's first rewrite the left-hand side (LHS) without the rightmost term:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{a^{3}(b+c)} + \\frac{1}{b^{3}(c+a)} + \\frac{1}{c^{3}(a+b)}\n   \\]\n   and subtract the given terms on the right side:\n   \\[\n   - \\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\frac{a(c-b)^{2}}{c+b} + \\frac{b(c-a)^{2}}{c+a} + \\frac{c(b-a)^{2}}{b+a}\\right].\n   \\]\n\n3. Introduce variables for simplification:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha = ac + ab, \\quad \\beta = bc + ab, \\quad \\gamma = ac + bc.\n   \\]\n\n4. Use these variables to perform the substitution:\n   \\[\n   ab = \\frac{\\alpha + \\beta - \\gamma}{2}, \\quad bc = \\frac{\\beta + \\gamma - \\alpha}{2}, \\quad ca = \\frac{\\alpha + \\gamma - \\beta}{2}.\n   \\]\n   So we have:\n   \\[\n   ac - ab = \\gamma - \\beta,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   bc - ab = \\gamma - \\alpha,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   ca - ab = \\alpha - \\beta.\n   \\]\n\n5. Substitute these into the expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(b^2 c^2)}{ab + ac} + \\frac{(c^2 a^2)}{bc + ba} + \\frac{(a^2 b^2)}{ac + bc} - \\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\frac{(ac - ab)^2}{ac + ab} + \\frac{(bc - ab)^2}{bc + ab} + \\frac{(ca - ba)^2}{ca + ba}\\right].\n   \\]\n\n6. We simplify further:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(\\beta + \\gamma - \\alpha)^2}{4\\alpha} + \\frac{(\\alpha + \\gamma - \\beta)^2}{4\\beta} + \\frac{(\\alpha + \\beta - \\gamma)^2}{4\\gamma}\n   \\]\n   subtracting\n   \\[\n   -\\left[ \\frac{(\\beta - \\gamma)^2}{4\\alpha} + \\frac{(\\alpha - \\gamma)^2}{4\\beta} + \\frac{(\\alpha - \\beta)^2}{4\\gamma} \\right].\n   \\]\n\n7. Combining these and simplifyi