ucture:**\n   - Uses each digit 0-6 exactly once.\n   - First digit \u2260 0.\n\n2. **Divisibility by 2 (First and Last Two Digits):**\n   - Last digit (position 7) must be even. Since the last two digits (positions 6-7) must be divisible by 2, and the entire number's last digit is 0 (ensuring divisibility by 10), position 7 is **0**.\n   - First two digits (positions 1-2) must be even. Position 2 must be even (2, 4, 6).\n\n3. **Divisibility by 5 (First and Last Five Digits):**\n   - First five digits end at position 5, which must be 5 (since 0 is already used). Thus, position 5 = **5**.\n   - Last five digits (positions 3-7) end with 0, satisfying divisibility by 5.\n\n4. **Divisibility by 3 (First and Last Three Digits):**\n   - Sum of first three digits (positions 1-3) must be divisible by 3.\n   - Sum of last three digits (positions 5-7 = 5, x, 0) must be divisible by 3. Hence, 5 + x + 0 \u2261 0 mod 3 \u21d2 x = 1 or 4. Thus, position 6 = **4** (as 1 leads to a contradiction in later steps).\n\n5. **Remaining Digits Assignment:**\n   - Used digits: 0, 4, 5. Remaining: 1, 2, 3, 6 for positions 1-4.\n   - Position 2 must be even \u21d2 2 or 6.\n\n6. **Subcases for Position 2:**\n   - **Case 1 (Position 2 = 2):**\n     - Remaining digits: 1, 3, 6 for positions 1, 3, 4.\n     - Valid permutations ensuring divisibility by 3 and 4 lead to the sequence 3, 2, 1, 6 in positions 1-4.\n   - **Case 2 (Position 2 = 6):**\n     - No valid permutations due to failed divisibility by 4.\n\n7. **Final Check for Divisibility by 6 (First and Last Six Digits):**\n   - First six digits (321654): Divisible by 2 (ends with 4) and 3 (sum = 21).\n   - Last six digits (216540): Divisible by 2 (ends with 0) and 3 (sum = 18).\n\n**Final Number:**  \nAfter verifying all conditions, the only valid number is **3216540**.", "ground_truth_solution": "\nWe need to find all seven-digit numbers that use each of the digits from 0 to 6 exactly once and satisfy a series of divisibility conditions.\n\