=1972.\n\nSo to get 1972, we need to get 3944 first, which is 394 appended with4, then divide by2.\n\nTo get 394, similarly:\n\n394= (10x +4)/2^k. Let's solve for k and x:\n\n394*2^k -4 must be divisible by10.\n\n394 mod10=4. So 4*2^k -4 \u22610 mod10.\n\n4*2^k \u22614 mod10 \u21922^k \u22611 mod5.\n\n2^4=16\u22611 mod5. So k=4.\n\nThus, 394*2^4 -4=394*16 -4=6304-4=6300. 6300/10=630.\n\nSo x=630.\n\nThus, 10*630 +4=6304. Divide by2 four times:6304/2=3152, /2=1576, /2=788, /2=394.\n\nThus, to get394, we need to get6304, which is630 appended with4, then divide by2 four times.\n\nTo get630:\n\n630= (10x +4)/2^k.\n\n630*2^k -4 must be divisible by10.\n\n630 mod10=0. So0*2^k -4\u2261-4\u22616 mod10. So 6\u22610 mod10? No. Wait, 630*2^k -4 \u22610 mod10 \u2192 (0*2^k -4)\u2261-4\u22616 mod10\u22600. So no solution. Therefore, need to append0 instead of4.\n\nIf we append0 to630, get6300. Divide by2:3150. Divide by2:1575. But1575 is odd. Not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, append0 to630 to get6300, then divide by2 twice:6300\u21923150\u21921575. Not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, append4 to630 get6304, divide by2 four times to get394.\n\nBut how to get630? Let's apply the same method.\n\nFor630:\n\nSolve 10x +4=630*2^k. So630*2^k -4 must be divisible by10.\n\n630 mod10=0. So0*2^k -4\u2261-4\u22616 mod10. Not 0. So need to append0 instead.\n\nAppend0 to63 to get630. So x=63.\n\nThus,630=63 appended with0. Then to get63:\n\n63 is odd. Must be obtained by dividing126 by2. 126 is even.\n\n126 can be obtained by appending0 or4 to12 or13.\n\n126 ends with6. So can't be obtained by appending0 or4. Therefore, must be obtained by dividing252 by2.\n\n252 ends with2. Must come from504.\n\n504 ends with4. Can be obtained by appending4 to50. So50 appended with4\u2192504. Then divide by2 to get252, divide by2 to get126, divide by2 to get63.\n\nSo path:\n\n4 \u2192 ... \u219250 \u2192504 \u2192252 \u2192126 \u219263.\n\nBut how to get50? Let's see.\n\n50 can be obtained by appending0 to5.\n\n5 is 