 y\u00b2 \u2248 0\n\nRearranged:\n\ny\u00b2 - 20y + 0.12 = 0\n\nSolve for y:\n\ny = [20 \u00b1 sqrt(400 - 4*1*0.12)] / 2\n\n= [20 \u00b1 sqrt(400 - 0.48)] / 2\n\n= [20 \u00b1 sqrt(399.52)] / 2\n\nsqrt(399.52) \u2248 19.988\n\nSo,\n\ny \u2248 [20 \u00b1 19.988]/2\n\nWe need positive y, so take the smaller root:\n\ny \u2248 [20 - 19.988]/2 \u2248 0.012/2 \u2248 0.006\n\nThus, y \u2248 0.006. But y = \u03b8\u00b2, so \u03b8 \u2248 sqrt(0.006) \u2248 0.0774597 radians\n\nThen, \u03b8 = 2\u03c0/n \u2248 0.0774597\n\nTherefore, n \u2248 2\u03c0 / 0.0774597 \u2248 6.28319 / 0.0774597 \u2248 81.05\n\nSo, approximately 81.05. So n \u2248 81. So perhaps 81 sides would be sufficient. But again, since this is an approximate method, maybe the actual n is a bit higher. Let me check with n=81 and n=80.\n\nCompute the exact ratio for n=81:\n\nA_p / A_c = (81 / (2\u03c0)) sin(2\u03c0/81)\n\nCompute 2\u03c0/81 \u2248 6.283185307 / 81 \u2248 0.077570189 radians\n\nCompute sin(0.077570189). Let's calculate it:\n\nsin(x) \u2248 x - x\u00b3/6 + x^5/120\n\nx \u2248 0.077570189\n\nx\u00b3 \u2248 0.077570189^3 \u2248 0.07757^3 \u2248 0.07757 * 0.07757 = 0.006017, then *0.07757 \u2248 0.0004666\n\nx\u00b3/6 \u2248 0.0004666 / 6 \u2248 0.00007777\n\nx^5 \u2248 0.0004666 * x\u00b2 \u2248 0.0004666 * 0.006017 \u2248 0.000002808\n\nx^5 / 120 \u2248 0.000002808 / 120 \u2248 0.0000000234\n\nSo sin(x) \u2248 0.077570189 - 0.00007777 + 0.0000000234 \u2248 0.07749244\n\nTherefore, (81 / (2\u03c0)) * 0.07749244 \u2248 (81 / 6.283185307) * 0.07749244 \u2248 12.89115 * 0.07749244 \u2248 1.0 (Wait, wait, let's compute more accurately.)\n\nWait, (81 / (2\u03c0)) = 81 / 6.283185307 \u2248 12.89115\n\nMultiply by sin(x) \u2248 0.07749244:\n\n12.89115 * 0.07749244 \u2248 Let's compute 12 * 0.077 = 0.924, 0.89115 * 0.077 \u2248 0.0686, so total approx 0.924 + 0.0686 = 0.9926, but wait, that can't be right.\n\nWait, no: 12.89115 multiplied by 0.07749244. Let me compute 12.89115 * 0.07 = 0.9023805, 12.89115 * 0