\n\nS(k) = (10/81)*(10^k*(9k - 1) + 1)\n\nWait, let me verify this formula for small k.\n\nFor k=1:\n\nS(1)=9*1*1=9\n\nUsing the formula: (10/81)*(10^1*(9*1 -1)+1) = (10/81)*(10*(8)+1)= (10/81)*(81)=10. But S(1)=9. Hmm, discrepancy here. So maybe the formula is slightly different.\n\nAlternatively, another approach.\n\nLet\u2019s consider S(k) = sum_{i=1}^k 9*10^{i-1}*i\n\nLet\u2019s denote S = 9* sum_{i=1}^k i*10^{i-1}\n\nWe can compute this sum using calculus or generating functions.\n\nLet\u2019s recall that sum_{i=1}^k i*r^{i-1} = (1 - (k+1)r^k + kr^{k+1}) ) / (1 - r)^2, for r \u22601.\n\nIn our case, r=10. Therefore,\n\nsum_{i=1}^k i*10^{i-1} = (1 - (k+1)10^k + k*10^{k+1}) / (1 -10)^2\n\n= (1 - (k+1)10^k + k*10^{k+1}) / 81\n\n= (1 - (k+1)10^k + 10k*10^{k}) /81\n\n= (1 + (10k -k -1)10^k)/81\n\n= (1 + (9k -1)10^k)/81\n\nTherefore,\n\nS(k) =9*sum_{i=1}^k i*10^{i-1} =9* [ (1 + (9k -1)10^k)/81 ]\n\n= [1 + (9k -1)10^k ] /9\n\nSo,\n\nS(k) = ( (9k -1)10^k +1 ) /9\n\nTherefore, the formula is S(k) = [ (9k -1)10^k +1 ] /9\n\nLet me check this formula with k=1:\n\nS(1)= [ (9*1 -1)10^1 +1 ] /9 = (8*10 +1)/9=(81)/9=9, which is correct. For k=2:\n\nsum_{i=1}^2 9*10^{i-1}*i =9*1*1 +9*2*10=9 + 180=189\n\nUsing the formula: [ (9*2 -1)10^2 +1 ] /9 = (17*100 +1)/9=(1701)/9=189. Correct.\n\nGreat, so the formula holds.\n\nTherefore, S(k) = [ (9k -1)10^k +1 ] /9\n\nSo, given that, we can compute S(k-1) and S(k) and check where 10^{1987} falls.\n\nWe need to find k such that S(k-1) <10^{1987} <=S(k)\n\nSo,\n\nS(k-1)= [ (9(k-1) -1)10^{k-1} +1 ] /9 = [ (9k -10)10^{k-1} +1 ] /9\n\nAnd S(k)= [ (9k -1)10^k +1 ] /9\n\nTherefore, we need:\n\n[ (9(k-1) -1)10^{k-1} +1 ] /9 <10^{1987} <=[ (9k -1)10^k +1 ] /9\n\nMultiply all parts by 9:\n\n(9(k-1) -1)10^{k-1} +1 <9*10^{1987} <=(9k -1)10^k +1\n\nFor large k, the \"+1\" is negligible, so approximate:\n\n(9k -10)10^{k-1} <9*10^{1987} <=(9k -1)10^k\n\nDivide all parts by 10^{k-1}:\n\n9k -10 <9*10^{1987 - (k-1)} <=(9k -1)10\n\nWhich simplifies to:\